RTM Test Harness
================

For the complete operator procedure, suite options, manual workflows, and
troubleshooting guide, see ``docs/TEST_PROCEDURE.md``.

The harness is a small pytest suite that passively listens to the rig's UDP
traffic on the host PC. Automated scenarios can drive RUN/RST through the
Teensy rig controller. Controller power-cycle, SD protocol swaps, and thermal
stimulus remain manual-assisted.

Layout
------
- ``test/rig/parser.py``       — wire frame → typed dataclass
- ``test/rig/monitor.py``      — UDP listener thread + frame queue
- ``test/rig/assertions.py``   — ``wait_for`` / ``expect`` helpers
- ``test/rig/scenario.py``     — shared live-rig scenario helpers
- ``test/scenarios/``          — pytest scenarios (one file per S-numbered case)
- ``test/log/<YYYY>/<MM>/<DD>/<HHMMSS>_pytest.log`` — per-session log

Network setup
-------------
- ClearCore: ``10.0.0.10``
- XPB:       ``10.0.0.11``
- Host PC:   ``10.0.0.100``  (must be set on the interface bound to the rig)
- Production UDP port:  ``8888``
- Observer UDP port:    ``8889``

The monitor sends a lightweight observer beacon once per second to CC and XPB
on port 8888. While the beacon is fresh, both boards tee directed-broadcast
debug copies on port 8889, so a single UDP bind on the PC sees both directions
through any unmanaged switch. If the PC or harness is absent, the boards use
only the production CC↔XPB unicast path.

Running
-------
From repo root:

::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -m "not manual"

  Smoke run:

  ::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -m smoke

  Manual-assisted runs need ``-s`` so prompts can read stdin:

  ::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/test_cold_boot_protocol_upload.py -v -s

  Run all manual-assisted scenarios (including any ``manual_power``,
  ``manual_protocol``, and ``manual_thermal`` subgroup tests):

  ::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -s -m "manual"

  Run manual subgroup slices:

  ::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -s -m "manual_power"
    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -s -m "manual_protocol"
    python -m pytest test/scenarios/ -v -s -m "manual_thermal"

  Manual protocol/thermal safety gate:

  ::

    During SD swap workflows, the harness now requires typed confirmation
    tokens before reset-driven validation begins:
      - protocol swap: type SWAPPED
      - thermal preheat: type READY
    This prevents false failures while the SD card is intentionally removed
    or XPB is still rebooting.

  Thermal scenario mode toggle:

  ::

    python -m pytest test/scenarios/test_manual_thermal_preheat.py -v -s --manual-thermal-mode body
    python -m pytest test/scenarios/test_manual_thermal_preheat.py -v -s --manual-thermal-mode external

  Use ``--rig-port`` to override the observer capture port and
  ``--rig-firmware-port`` to override the board control/beacon port.
  Smoke-marked scenarios run first during the full automated suite. By default,
  a smoke failure or skip stops the session before later automated tests run;
  pass ``--no-smoke-gate`` only when intentionally collecting more failures.

Markers:

- ``live_rig`` — requires the rig to be powered and on the network.
- ``smoke``    — short live-rig confidence path.
- ``full``     — automated full-regression scenario.
- ``stateful`` — mutates physical rig state and self-normalizes preconditions.
- ``requires_hlfb_quick`` — expects the ``HLFB_QUICK`` protocol baseline.
- ``manual``   — requires operator action.
- ``manual_power`` — manual controller power-cycle or unplug/replug.
- ``manual_protocol`` — manual SD protocol swap or edit.
- ``manual_thermal`` — manual thermal stimulus or supervision.
- ``slow``     — long-running scenarios.

Current manual scenarios:

- ``test_cold_boot_protocol_upload.py``
- ``test_manual_power_loss_resume.py``
- ``test_manual_protocol_swap.py``
- ``test_manual_thermal_preheat.py``

Skip the manual ones with ``-m "not manual"``.

Conventions
-----------
- Each test gets a fresh ``Monitor`` (function scope) — frame buffer and clock
  start at zero per test.
- Stateful automated tests normalize the physical rig state before asserting
  behavior. Collection order is for readable transcripts, not correctness.
- Pass/fail is determined from observable UDP telemetry (``HB;STATE=…``,
  ``STAT;…``, ``NOTICE;…``, ``PR_*``) — never from internal firmware state.
- ``test_protocol_upload.py`` is passive and order-tolerant: ``RUNNING``,
  ``PAUSED``, or ``COMPLETED`` heartbeats count as proof that a protocol was
  already loaded/executed. Use ``test_reset_reloads_protocol.py`` for the
  deterministic reset-to-upload chain.
- Reset-gate checks wait for both ``NOTICE;PROTO_RX=OK`` and a later ``IDLE``
  heartbeat. ``PROTO_RX=OK`` can arrive several seconds before CC finishes
  the post-reset ``BOOTING`` window.
- On failure, dump the last N frames so the log file is enough to diagnose.
